WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
DeepMind launches an institute to study AGI's economic, scientific, and societal effects with 20-plus years of prior discussion behind it. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 176. Demis Hassabis announced the launch of the DeepMind Institute to expand interdisciplinary research on AGI's potential impact on the economy, science, and society. The institute builds on more than 20 years of discussions between Hassabis and Shane Legg

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:35.080
about these topics. The effort aims to spur the discussions needed to get the next steps

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:41.640
right in the AI era. Hassab is also received the Albert Medal from the RSA, noting that

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.980
arts and humanities will be crucial in shaping the future society once in the AGI era.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.040
He highlighted a fun discussion with Stephen Fry covering many new topics in the AGI context.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:59.700
Dantanox is an open source Jack's Flax Library with a single modular transformer backbone

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:05.860
that supports auto-regressive decoding, discrete mask diffusion, and continuous flow matching.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.860
Switching paradigms, attention mechanisms, or hardware topology requires only a configuration

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:16.860
change while keeping the backbone, tokenizer, and training infrastructure consistent.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:23.600
The library enables controlled cross-paradigm comparisons within one API for training, streaming

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.600
inference, and benchmarking.

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:31.820
MyoVox decodes open vocabulary English text from 31-channel surface electromiography

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:35.020
recorded from facial muscles during vocalized speech.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:44.240
It improves on the EMG2 speech general corpus from a published 51.17% word error rate to 18.53

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:50.180
percent, through bidirectional conformer training and Q-Lora fine-tuned language model re-ranking.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.540
The approach first recovers open vocabulary decode settings missing from the public release

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.000
to reach a faithful 40.63% word error rate baseline.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:06.460
A second step replaces the causal encoder with a bidirectional conformer trained by cross-modal

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:10.040
distillation against WAV-LM-LARGE layer 9 features.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:15.380
Prime scientists jointly determines research direction and resource investment across

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:22.000
successive research attempts using an executable plan tree and adaptive MCTS-based allocation

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:30.760
policy. Across 12 AI research tasks, it improves average reward by 10.3%, with 50.6% fewer

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:36.240
research attempts than auto-research under the same resource budget. The system treats strategic

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:40.980
research effort allocation as an explicit optimization target and preserves

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.560
competing plans and their outcomes across attempts in the planetary

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:49.440
representation. A controlled study evaluates supervised fine-tuning with

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:56.400
Laura, reinforcement learning via GRPO, and SFT followed by GRPO across six

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:03.820
QN3 models from 0.6 billion to 32 billion parameters. SFT with Laura is the

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:08.160
longest indistribution method in 15 out of 18 experimental settings.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:14.240
Laura outperforms full parameter fine tuning by better preserving pre-trained agentic behavior.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:21.340
On cross data set transfer, GRPO wins 29 out of 54 settings where training and test

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.140
data sets differ, but it's margin over SFT averages under one point.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:32.420
The RCA framework models stimulation interactions as a sequential decision process with protocol

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:38.280
constrained chain of cognition and inference time value alignment for safety and engagement goals.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:44.420
It improves protocol adherence, safety, and group facilitation over standard prompting baselines

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:51.040
across six backbone LLMs. The framework addresses data scarcity in privacy-sensitive low resource

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:57.260
languages such as Cantonese through STAR CS style transfer and role-condition synthesis.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:05.480
Aferi Psycho analyzes 1,415 turn-1 correct model language item observations from 100 source

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:09.480
questions across 7 open-weight checkpoints and 6 languages.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:15.620
A assertive framing increases target selection by 30.4 percentage points, while verification

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:18.360
decreases it by 17.4 points.

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:24.540
The effect remains 34.8 points among observations correct after option reordering.

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:32.540
Motowansnan provides 1,271 sentence-aligned pairs manually translated from Wolloth into

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.360
modern-standard Arabic, drawn from the Masaka-Nare corpus.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:47.540
Fine-tuning Afri-NLLB12 on the corpus yields 7.76 BLEU and 30.72 Chris F++ for Wolloth

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:48.040
to Arabic.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:05:00.100
The Corpus is released under CC by NC on Hugging Face and Github, and the source texts cover politics, society, religion, and sports in Senegalese News Discourse.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:11.540
Lex EN is a human adjudicated correction layer over Maru 2022's All-Underscore New Benchmark, with 211 labels changed and 56 removed.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:21.140
Frontier LLMs converge near 95% accuracy on Lex EN version 1, with the best at 95.6%.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:29.200
Glite Lens, a 298 million-parameter buy-in-coder trained on repaired labels, reaches 83.6

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:33.160
Ragnato All, and 87.4 Maru All New.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:39.200
Examine the Dantonox library to run controlled comparisons across auto-regressive, diffusion,

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.740
and flow matching paradigms, without changing tokenizers or training code.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.160
Test the RCA agent framework on cognitive stimulation tasks

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:52.580
if you work with low resource dialogue data or elderly care applications.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:57.340
Fine-tune AFRI-NLLB variants on the Moodle1Snon-Corpus

00:05:57.340 --> 00:06:00.520
to measure gains on wool-off Arabic translation directions.

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.300
Run the Lex-EN benchmark harness to see how frontier models perform

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.200
on corrected word-sense labels versus older gold standards.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:15.420
SAM Altman indicated the main open AI launch originally planned for this week will arrive

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.520
next week instead.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:23.340
Open AI plans to track model misalignment regularly after flagging new concerning AI behavior.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:28.680
Further details on the DeepMind Institute's research agenda are expected in coming weeks.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:34.100
We can pop the hood on how language models handle factual recall by separating relation

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:40.200
on set from Entity Commitment. Language models retrieve relation type information such as capital

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:46.820
of before they commit to specific entity answers such as France to Paris. The temporal asymmetry

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:52.880
holds across four decoder-only models and eight prompt families, with relation on set preceding

00:06:52.880 --> 00:07:00.440
entity on set by 10 to 16 layers at a 0.4 threshold. Entity information is already present in early

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:05.320
layers, yet remains generation-controlling only after it roots to the final token.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:11.580
This separation means activation-steering interventions aimed at entity facts nust target later

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.840
layers than those used for relation facts.

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:19.380
When the routing step is the bottleneck, simply increasing early-layer entity patching yields

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.900
little additional accuracy.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:27.660
The ordering holds across all 16 model threshold combinations for thresholds between 0.2 and

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:28.580
0.5.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:35.580
Entity token patching succeeds at 90% to 100% in early layers even though commitment is deferred.

